/T (The Random Forest ensemble was successfully implemented on the Breast Cancer dataset. It achieved a test accuracy of 95.61% \(OOB score 95.38%, ROC-AUC 0.9937\), higher than the 91.23% of a single Decision Tree, and the 5-fold cross-validation accuracy was also higher \(95.61% against 91.73%\). The accuracy became stable from 25 trees onwards, and worst area, worst concave points and worst radius were the most important features. Hyperparameter tuning raised the cross-validation accuracy to 96.04% while the test accuracy stayed at 95.61%.)
/E (The Random Forest ensemble was successfully implemented on the Breast Cancer dataset. It achieved a test accuracy of 95.61% \(OOB score 95.38%, ROC-AUC 0.9937\), higher than the 91.23% of a single Decision Tree, and the 5-fold cross-validation accuracy was also higher \(95.61% against 91.73%\). The accuracy became stable from 25 trees onwards, and worst area, worst concave points and worst radius were the most important features. Hyperparameter tuning raised the cross-validation accuracy to 96.04% while the test accuracy stayed at 95.61%.)
